    {
      "id": "17862090",
      "title": "Using Custom \"ng generate\" Schematics",
      "lectureOrder": 742,
      "videoOrder": 682,
      "sourceHash": "7c0437bf3ff05db056e071ac3bf9073c3b2cdaf401723bcc99482e2d4bc6f6a6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.38,
          "en": "Instructor: Now let's start with NG generate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.38,
          "end": 5.85,
          "en": "We know NG generate, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 8.4,
          "en": "We can use it in any Angular project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.4,
          "end": 10.47,
          "en": "That is because Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.47,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "and the Angular CLI has some default blueprints included.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "For example, for generating a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 19.41,
          "en": "for generating a pipe, a service, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.41,
          "end": 22.02,
          "en": "So these are basically schematics or support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.02,
          "end": 25.35,
          "en": "for the NG generate schematic that is already built in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 26.61,
          "en": "But you could add your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.61,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "And third party packages can also add their own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 31.803,
          "en": "not just for NG ad but also for NG generate.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.803,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "For example, with Angular material installed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 40.67,
          "en": "we can run NG generate @Angular slash materials.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.34,
          "end": 44.37,
          "en": "So basically the the name of the schematic provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.37,
          "end": 47.55,
          "en": "by default, if you leave this empty, it's the default seal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.55,
          "end": 49.08,
          "en": "the default Angular set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.08,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "but you can override it and use a different one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "In this case the Angualr material package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 57.48,
          "en": "Colon, then a name of a supported schematic and the,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.48,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "for example, naf.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 61.2,
          "en": "And of course in the official docs of Angular material",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.2,
          "end": 62.25,
          "en": "in this case you learn all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.25,
          "end": 66.81,
          "en": "about the NG generate schematics it added and you can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.81,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "So here we can use nav and then a name where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 72.87,
          "en": "we want to create our, in this case navigation setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 72.87,
          "end": 74.4,
          "en": "And if I hit enter now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 74.4,
          "end": 76.77,
          "en": "this uses this generate schematic provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 76.77,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "by Angular material, and it adds a new component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "So under the hood it probably uses NG generate component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "but it adds a new component, which is not empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 87.93,
          "en": "but which has a different default blueprint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.93,
          "end": 90.33,
          "en": "In this case, you see it has a blueprint where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.33,
          "end": 95.293,
          "en": "we have a side navigation controller, a toolbar, a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 95.293,
          "end": 98.67,
          "en": "and then also can show some content here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.67,
          "end": 101.434,
          "en": "like maybe in a main block.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 101.434,
          "end": 104.00999999999999,
          "en": "Simple H2 header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.00999999999999,
          "end": 105.12,
          "en": "This works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.12,
          "end": 108.57,
          "en": "And now let's include this main nav component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.57,
          "end": 109.5,
          "en": "in app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 109.5,
          "end": 112.95,
          "en": "Let's use main nav like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.95,
          "end": 114.50999999999999,
          "en": "Make sure that an app module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 114.50999999999999,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "this was added to declarations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 118.05,
          "en": "And if we now run NG serve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 120.99,
          "en": "you will see a nice navigation which works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.99,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "out of the box using Angular material components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 126.75,
          "en": "Thanks to this custom schematic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 126.75,
          "end": 128.61,
          "en": "this NG generate schematic added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 128.61,
          "end": 130.8,
          "en": "by the Angular material package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.8,
          "end": 132.57,
          "en": "And you could build something like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.57,
          "end": 134.7,
          "en": "on your own as well if you wanted to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 134.7,
          "end": 135.533,
          "en": "But as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 135.533,
          "end": 137.76,
          "en": "a lot of third party packages support it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 137.76,
          "end": 142.05,
          "en": "So this adds on to the default schematics you already have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 142.05,
          "end": 144.6,
          "en": "in a Angular project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 144.6,
          "end": 146.34,
          "en": "And of course here we got an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 146.34,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "because it's not main nav, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 151.82999999999998,
          "en": "it's app main nav, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 151.82999999999998,
          "end": 154.77,
          "en": "We can of course check the the selector here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 154.77,
          "end": 156.24,
          "en": "So little oversight from my side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 156.24,
          "end": 157.71,
          "en": "Let me fix this app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 157.71,
          "end": 161.59,
          "en": "And after fixing this, if you visit local host 4,200",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.07999999999998,
          "end": 166.07999999999998,
          "en": "we get this nice little application here where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 166.07999999999998,
          "end": 167.37,
          "en": "of course not much is happening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 167.37,
          "end": 169.53,
          "en": "but where we now could build up on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 169.53,
          "end": 171.54,
          "en": "to build an application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 171.54,
          "end": 174.09,
          "en": "So this is the ng generate schematic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 174.09,
          "end": 176.57999999999998,
          "en": "and what you have built into the CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 176.57999999999998,
          "end": 177.69,
          "en": "and the default project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 177.69,
          "end": 180.51,
          "en": "and how third party packages as well as yourself",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 180.51,
